From dd89cf90a53b470fac10b8e3e57163b01ba3aa5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Delgado <328510259+thinkddr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:09:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ios): derive canvas geometry from the attached view

Measure the attached view bounds, rendering scale and safe-area insets, and
refresh them when layout, safe areas or scene orientation change. Send the
already oriented drawable dimensions to Go without a second landscape swap.
Use the same view coordinate space and scale for touches. Convert keyboard
rectangles from the screen coordinate space; only full-width docked overlap
reserves the canvas bottom edge.

Include 24 portable geometry/keyboard cases and source contracts. The real
Go/Fyne/UIKit app was compiled and linked for device and simulator with
Xcode 27.0, then exercised on iPhone and iPad iOS 27.0 simulators across
rotation cycles and full, half, offset-small and restored-full viewports,
with 32 native taps. See the source PR and CI for the retained UIKit harness.

Base: v2.8.2-sytue.1 (62c88876f8c30d381abd4a53601b270485c205cb)
Source: dd89cf90a53b470fac10b8e3e57163b01ba3aa5d
PR: https://github.com/thinkddr/fyne/pull/5
CI: https://github.com/thinkddr/fyne/actions/runs/40196864106

This minimal export contains driver code, portable C regressions and source
contracts. Original driver copyright/BSD notices and new helper/regression
Apache-2.0 notices are preserved from the source. See FORK-NOTICE.md and
LICENSE-MODIFICATIONS in the source repository for the fork license terms.
